---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ChartGrammar from '../../../components/ChartGrammar.astro';
import { signs } from '../../../data/signs';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'The 12 Signs', href: '/explore/signs/' },
];
const elements = ['Fire', 'Earth', 'Air', 'Water'] as const;
const modalities = ['Cardinal', 'Fixed', 'Mutable'] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="The 12 Zodiac Signs. Styles of expression" description="The twelve zodiac signs describe styles of expression, not twelve kinds of people. Learn elements, modalities, rulers, and how signs modify planets and houses in context." path="/explore/signs/" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
        <h1>The signs answer: how does it express?</h1>
        <p class="lede">Signs describe style, not twelve kinds of people. Every chart contains all twelve signs. Their meaning becomes useful when you know what planet, house, ruler, or other chart factor is expressing through that style.</p>
      </div>
      <img class="hero__img" src={scenes.signs.src} srcset={scenes.signs.srcset} sizes="100vw" alt={scenes.signs.alt} width={scenes.signs.width} height={scenes.signs.height} fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ChartGrammar active="sign" />
      <div class="prose flow">
        <h2>See the system underneath the twelve names</h2>
        <p>The zodiac combines four elements with three modalities. That structure is more useful than memorizing twelve disconnected lists of traits. A sign tells you <em>how</em>; the planet tells you <em>what</em> is expressing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sign-matrix" role="table" aria-label="Signs by element and modality">
        <div class="sign-matrix__corner" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        {modalities.map((modality) => <div class="sign-matrix__header" role="columnheader">{modality}</div>)}
        {elements.map((element) => (
          <>
            <div class="sign-matrix__header" role="rowheader">{element}</div>
            {modalities.map((modality) => {
              const sign = signs.find((s) => s.element === element && s.modality === modality);
              return <div class="sign-matrix__cell" role="cell">{sign && <a href={`/explore/signs/${sign.slug}/`}><span aria-hidden="true">{sign.glyph}</span> <strong>{sign.name}</strong><span>{sign.keywords.join(' · ')}</span></a>}</div>;
            })}
          </>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="prose"><a href="/explore/elements-and-modalities/">Go deeper into how elements and modalities work.</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>A sign is a modifier</h2>
      <p>Venus in Aries and Saturn in Aries share a cardinal-fire style without doing the same job. Keep asking what is expressing through the sign, where in life it is operating, and what relationships modify it. That is more revealing than asking what a sign is "like" in isolation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sign-matrix { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(4.5rem, .65fr) repeat(3, minmax(8rem, 1fr)); gap: 1px; margin-block: var(--space-8); overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border-color, currentColor); }
  .sign-matrix__header, .sign-matrix__corner, .sign-matrix__cell { padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border-color, currentColor); }
  .sign-matrix__header { font-weight: 700; }
  .sign-matrix__cell a { display: flex; min-height: 7rem; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: var(--space-2); text-decoration: none; }
  .sign-matrix__cell a > span:last-child { font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .sign-matrix { font-size: var(--text-sm); } .sign-matrix__header, .sign-matrix__corner, .sign-matrix__cell { padding: var(--space-3); } }
</style>
